    {
      "id": "c1642873-249c-466c-b794-b34cd1f136cc",
      "name": "Blog",
      "path": "WWW / Blog",
      "docTypeId": "d61d96e3-b2ca-49e0-916c-424b268550ec",
      "templateId": "01c48934-4df6-4034-9022-489319fafdbe",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [
        {
          "domainName": "/",
          "isoCode": "en-US"
        }
      ],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "title",
          "value": "The MCP Blog"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "intro",
          "value": "Notes on the Model Context Protocol: why it is awesome, how it works, and what it means for the sites we build. Two posts, zero fluff."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "body",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "41242388-3d7d-4b21-84f6-af2375e2efc0",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "ed82bac2-3ea8-427e-ba62-41f7c2032f10",
                "key": "41242388-3d7d-4b21-84f6-af2375e2efc0",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>Welcome to the MCP Blog — a small site built to show what happens when a CMS speaks the Model Context Protocol. Every page here was modeled, filled and published through MCP tools.</p><p>Start with the two posts below, or poke around the backoffice: the schema, the media library and the content tree tell the same story.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "41242388-3d7d-4b21-84f6-af2375e2efc0",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "urls": [
        "/",
        "https://localhost:44317/"
      ],
      "docType": "blogFrontPage",
      "template": "blogFrontPage"
    },
    {
      "id": "d29d0e12-4338-41a1-972a-692386a1c8c3",
      "name": "Why MCP Is Awesome: One Protocol, Every Tool",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Why MCP Is Awesome: One Protocol, Every Tool",
      "docTypeId": "35628c7c-7964-4d3c-9be5-0e79c49411d1",
      "templateId": "0347d920-8894-443a-8ea9-94f6cf19ac47",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "title",
          "value": "Why MCP Is Awesome: One Protocol, Every Tool"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.DateTime",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "publishDate",
          "value": "2026-10-01 09:00:00"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "excerpt",
          "value": "The Model Context Protocol turns scattered, bespoke integrations into one discoverable toolset. Here is why that changes how we build software — and how we ship sites."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "listingImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "a6df3243-a8a3-433c-bc1b-33e11f9323c4",
              "mediaKey": "d933630c-f8af-4e27-bb39-efe88db3fd00",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "body",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "82a4407c-86a1-43ab-89be-209be83fc2cb",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "bd51ea4d-f435-4e26-8089-b1b24895f970",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "6caf57d5-be72-47b7-b64d-bb75490d88f6",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "37170480-be36-4e73-ad05-a897d3032b62",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "ed82bac2-3ea8-427e-ba62-41f7c2032f10",
                "key": "82a4407c-86a1-43ab-89be-209be83fc2cb",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>Ask ten developers how they wire an AI assistant to their tools and you will get ten different answers: a bespoke REST client here, a GraphQL wrapper there, a pile of shell scripts nobody dares to touch. The Model Context Protocol, or MCP, replaces that zoo with a single, open standard.</p><p>MCP defines one simple contract: a server exposes tools, resources and prompts; a client — an AI assistant, an IDE, a CMS — discovers them and calls them. No more per-integration glue code. Write the server once and every MCP-capable client can use it.</p><p>What makes it awesome is not the protocol itself but what it unlocks. Tools become composable. Your editor, your terminal and your deployment pipeline can share the same capabilities, because they all speak the same language.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "8244f782-cba8-4bd4-ae19-385d177277b7",
                "key": "bd51ea4d-f435-4e26-8089-b1b24895f970",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "27d5a08c-66d1-4ca1-9caf-7a8825697cc6",
                        "mediaKey": "e86c8f93-24bd-4075-b867-f806f472c675",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "Every node connected: MCP turns isolated tools into a network. Photo by Conny Schneider on Unsplash."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "ed82bac2-3ea8-427e-ba62-41f7c2032f10",
                "key": "6caf57d5-be72-47b7-b64d-bb75490d88f6",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>On this very site, the Umbraco MCP server models the schema, imports the media and publishes the pages — all through the same protocol this post is praising. Document types, data types, templates, domains: created, verified and wired together without a single hand-written migration file.</p><p>The practical win is speed with safety. Because every operation goes through Umbraco's own management API, validation still runs, uSync still exports, and the content tree stays the single source of truth. MCP does not bypass the CMS; it finally gives the CMS a front door that assistants can walk through.</p><p>If you are building anything with AI in 2026, bet on MCP. The ecosystem is growing daily, and the protocol is simple enough to implement in an afternoon.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "d6dd18e9-57af-4f5d-af6f-199e4bd6fc33",
                "key": "37170480-be36-4e73-ad05-a897d3032b62",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "quote",
                    "value": "MCP is the USB-C of AI integrations: one port, every device, no more dongle drawer."
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "attribution",
                    "value": "The MCP Blog"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "82a4407c-86a1-43ab-89be-209be83fc2cb",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "bd51ea4d-f435-4e26-8089-b1b24895f970",
